ient_impl.h. Is it really necessary for the API to…"],["31f2fd33_df7565d2",27,-32,1,"nit: I'd do a func-local `using WindowShowState = ui::mojom::blink::WindowShowState;` -- this might simplify the switch too"],["422912d7_21ad8b67",22,-32,1,"nit: `using ui::mojom::blink::WindowShowState` in the anon namespace"],["123ba98d_a5da251f",24,-31,1,"optional nit: extract shared script string literals or test helper methods I suggest a helper that takes the API method name and expected state, e.g.: ``` EvalJsResult EvalDisplayStateChange( const…"],["245c2538_0eefb872",27,-31,1,"Clients like WebViewImpl would be better served be a single notification of window state change (as I suggested above). Then WebViewImpl can decide how to resolve its own callbacks from the clearest…"],["51607962_2864f238",22,-31,1,"This represents success for any of the operations, not just maximized ```suggestion const String& error_message, bool result) { ```"],["5e1ff81f_25c5e137",26,-31,1,"This is a great improvement over the initial impl, thank you. Still, this won't work really well when a sequence of JS methods are invoked, then promises are resolved out of order e.g. `m1 =…"],["88493cd2_82ed86a7",28,-31,1,"Consider adding a single `OnWindowShowStateChanged(ui::mojom::blink::WindowShowState)` instead."],["8cbef840_6ddc4fdc",27,-31,1,"There's no clear request denial signal at this layer, right? If so, when the WM silently ignores a request, the JS promise will hang indefinitely. I wonder if the promises should reject with some…"],["1d8af10d_587215dc",24,-2,0,"I wonder if any of these might need RunUntil (ditto elsewhere exiting fullscreen)"],["33f87095_4e45ec7b",24,-2,1,"optional nit: a helper method might be useful (this is done 3+ times), it's quite close to EvalDisplayStateChange, but creating a parallel fullscreen helper is likely better than generalizing a…"],["2052ef3c_ee88b207",22,-1,1,"Shorthand: `resolver->RejectWithDOMException(DOMExceptionCode::kNotAllowedError, error_message));`"],[